Project Background

The Knowledge Project is a joint initiative between UNDP’s Regional Bureau for Arab States (RBAS) and the Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum Knowledge Foundation (MBRF) established in 2008. It aims to promote knowledge societies and policies as transformational means to achieving sustainable development in the Arab States region and beyond. The project builds on the Arab Knowledge Reports, the Arab Knowledge Index, the Knowledge4All portal, the Arab Reading Index, the Knowledge Summit, the KnowTalks series, the Future of Knowledge Foresight Report series and the Global Knowledge Index (GKI), in addition to the Future Skills Academy.

In 2026, the Knowledge Project has a multifaceted work plan aimed at advancing its mission on multiple fronts. It is set to produce GKI 2026. Through the Future Skills Academy, the project is committed to reskilling and upskilling over 25,000 learners, empowering them with essential skills for the future. Additionally, the project is set to organize the Knowledge Summit and host a series of engaging KnowTalks events, providing platforms for thought leaders to discuss critical topics and disseminate valuable insights.

To enhance knowledge accessibility, the project is currently revamping the existing Knowledge4All portal and mobile application to improve the user experience. This major milestone will result in a platform that consolidates all project initiatives, ensuring timely and easy access to information for all users.

In addition to these efforts, the Knowledge Project will implement a robust outreach and dissemination strategy to maximize the impact of its project outputs, ensuring that its valuable resources reach a diverse and global audience.

Accordingly, the Knowledge Project is seeking the services of a Communications Intern, whose duties will include: developing, scheduling, and publishing bilingual English and Arabic content; assisting in producing multimedia assets and curating newsletters; managing social media platforms and the portal CMS. In addition, the intern will monitor channels, track performance using Google Analytics, maintain digital asset archives; and assist with editorial calendars, content creation, content translation, exploring the latest web trends, and general communications tasks.

Duties and Responsibilities

The intern will be based in the Dubai, UAE office. Responsibilities may include but will not be limited to the following:

- Contribute to the preparation of editorial and content calendars for the portal and related social platforms, as well as web content production.

- Assist with the preparation and dissemination of the Knowledge Project newsletter.

- Support the development, scheduling, and publishing of content across the Knowledge Project’s social media platforms, including LinkedIn, Instagram, Facebook, X, and YouTube.

- Draft engaging English and Arabic social media copy in line with brand guidelines and regional audiences, and produce multimedia content, including graphics, carousels, videos, and reels, to support digital communications campaigns and event live coverage.

- Upload, publish, and update content on the Knowledge4All portal and mobile app through the CMS.

- Regularly monitor online media coverage and mentions of Knowledge Project initiatives across different media outlets and digital platforms.

- Monitor social media channels, the Knowledge4All portal and mobile app, respond to comments, messages and inquiries as directed, and share user feedback and observations to support improvements to the user experience.

- Support web and social media analytics and performance reporting.

- Maintain and organize digital communications assets and support the compilation and archiving of Knowledge Project data, including news, photos, videos, and other project files.

- Assist with the translation of content between Arabic and English.

- Carry out other related support tasks as required.

